## Bridge and torch (bridge-and-torch): generated by spec_backend.py (WorldSpec, path B: Lean description, Python rules) from the instructor statements.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##  1. Four people must cross a bridge at night. They start on the near side.
##  2. They have one torch. Anyone on the bridge must have the torch with them.
##  3. At most two people can be on the bridge at once.
##  4. Crossing takes Ann 1 minute, Bob 2 minutes, Cy 5 minutes and Di 10 minutes.
##  5. Two people crossing together go at the speed of the slower one.
##  6. One or two people on the side with the torch can cross with the torch to the other side.
##  7. The goal is that all four people are on the far side within 17 minutes.
##
## Assumption ledger:
##   A-BT1: "Anyone on the bridge must have the torch": a crossing moves the torch with the people; the torch is at a side, like the people.
##   A-BT2: Elapsed minutes are a number on a clock object, starting at 0; each crossing adds its time with the new update effect.
##   A-BT3: "at the speed of the slower one": cross-two takes a faster person a and a slower person b (b.minutes > a.minutes) and adds b's minutes, so no maximum is needed and each pair is proposed once. All four times differ; equal times would need >= and would propose a pair twice.
##   A-BT4: "the other side": a static other relation between the two sides, both ways.
##   A-BT6: "within 17 minutes" asks for a fast crossing, so a crossing's minutes are also its step cost, and the task searches by cost (flags iterative-step cost, which brings cost-metric unit): iterative deepening on a cost cap, the library's IDA*. The clock still decides the losing state.
##   A-BT7: Search control, not from the English (as decided by JL on 16 Nov 2026 for the river crossings): a look-ahead state that returns to a situation already on its path fails. A situation is where each person and the torch are; the clock is not part of it, so going back and forth is cut off even though it changes the time.
##   A-BT5: "within 17 minutes": more than 17 elapsed minutes is a losing state; the goal itself tests only where the people are.

sp {bridge-and-torch*propose*initialize-bridge-and-torch
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-bridge-and-torch ^task-operator false)
}

sp {bridge-and-torch*apply*initialize-bridge-and-torch
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-bridge-and-torch ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name bridge-and-torch ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <k-near-side> <k-far-side> <k-torch> <k-clock> <k-ann> <k-bob> <k-cy> <k-di> <k-task>)
   (<k-near-side> ^object-handle near-side ^anchored true ^type bank ^name near-side)
   (<k-far-side> ^object-handle far-side ^anchored true ^type bank ^name far-side)
   (<k-torch> ^object-handle torch ^anchored true ^type torch ^name torch)
   (<k-clock> ^object-handle clock ^anchored true ^type clock ^name clock ^elapsed 0)
   (<k-ann> ^object-handle ann ^anchored true ^type person ^name ann ^minutes 1)
   (<k-bob> ^object-handle bob ^anchored true ^type person ^name bob ^minutes 2)
   (<k-cy> ^object-handle cy ^anchored true ^type person ^name cy ^minutes 5)
   (<k-di> ^object-handle di ^anchored true ^type person ^name di ^minutes 10)
   (<k-task> ^object-handle task ^anchored true ^type task)
   (<ds> ^desired-count 1 ^desired <d1>)
   (<d1> ^object <d1-o>)
   (<d1-o> ^object-handle task ^goal-met true)
   (<w> ^at <rel-1>)
   (<rel-1> ^argument1 <k-ann> ^argument2 <k-near-side>)
   (<w> ^at <rel-2>)
   (<rel-2> ^argument1 <k-bob> ^argument2 <k-near-side>)
   (<w> ^at <rel-3>)
   (<rel-3> ^argument1 <k-cy> ^argument2 <k-near-side>)
   (<w> ^at <rel-4>)
   (<rel-4> ^argument1 <k-di> ^argument2 <k-near-side>)
   (<w> ^at <rel-5>)
   (<rel-5> ^argument1 <k-torch> ^argument2 <k-near-side>)
   (<w> ^other <rel-6>)
   (<rel-6> ^argument1 <k-near-side> ^argument2 <k-far-side>)
   (<w> ^other <rel-7>)
   (<rel-7> ^argument1 <k-far-side> ^argument2 <k-near-side>)
   (log 1 (crlf) |Initialize bridge-and-torch.|)
}

